AbstractSheaf ^** RingElement -- tensor power of an abstract sheaf
******************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^**: (Macaulay2Doc)^_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        F^**n
  * Inputs:
      * F, an *note abstract sheaf: AbstractSheaf,, of rank 1 if n is not an
        integer
      * n, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, in (or promotable
        to) the intersection ring of the variety of $F$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract sheaf: AbstractSheaf,, the $n$-th tensor power of $F$

Description
===========

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : pt = base n                                |
|                                                |
|o1 = pt                                         |
|                                                |
|o1 : an abstract variety of dimension 0         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : X = abstractProjectiveSpace'(3,pt)         |
|                                                |
|o2 = X                                          |
|                                                |
|o2 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {3, 1}|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = intersectionRing X                     |
|                                                |
|o3 = A                                          |
|                                                |
|o3 : QuotientRing                               |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : ch ((OO_X(1)) ^** 2)                       |
|                                                |
|                2   4 3                         |
|o4 = 1 + 2h + 2h  + -h                          |
|                    3                           |
|                                                |
|o4 : A                                          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : ch ((OO_X(1)) ^** 3)                       |
|                                                |
|              9 2   9 3                         |
|o5 = 1 + 3h + -h  + -h                          |
|              2     2                           |
|                                                |
|o5 : A                                          |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : ch ((OO_X(1)) ^** n)                       |
|                                                |
|               1 2 2   1 3 3                    |
|o6 = 1 + n*h + -n h  + -n h                     |
|               2       6                        |
|                                                |
|o6 : A                                          |
+------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * "AbstractSheaf ^** QQ"
  * *note AbstractSheaf ^** RingElement: AbstractSheaf ^_st_st RingElement, --
    tensor power of an abstract sheaf
  * "AbstractSheaf ^** ZZ"
