abstractVariety(ZZ,Ring) -- make an abstract variety
****************************************************

  * Function: *note abstractVariety: abstractVariety_lpZZ_cmRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        abstractVariety(d,A)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * A, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, of degree length 1
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ReturnType => a *note type: (Macaulay2Doc)Type,, default value
        AbstractVariety, a type of AbstractVariety
      * DefaultIntegral => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract variety: AbstractVariety,, of dimension d whose
        intersection ring is A and whose *note class: (Macaulay2Doc)class, is
        the value of the ReturnType option
  * Consequences:
      * The ring A is altered so it knows what abstract variety it is
        associated with (see *note variety(Ring):
        (Varieties)variety_lpRing_rp,), preventing it from being used in this
        way more than once.  The methods for converting its elements to strings
        and nets are replaced by methods that display monomials of higher
        degree further to the right, parenthesizing multiple terms of the same
        degree.
      * Unless *note DefaultIntegral: abstractVariety_lpZZ_cmRing_rp, is set to
        false, a default method for integration of elements of the intersection
        ring is installed, which returns a formal *note expression:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Expression, representing the integral of the degree $d$
        part of the element when $d$ is greater than zero, and simply returns
        the degree 0 part of the element when $d$ is zero.

Description
===========

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = abstractVariety(3, QQ[c,d,Degrees=>{1,2}])|
|                                                   |
|o1 = X                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : an abstract variety of dimension 3            |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = abstractSheaf(X, ChernCharacter => 3+c+d) |
|                                                   |
|o2 = F                                             |
|                                                   |
|o2 : an abstract sheaf of rank 3 on X              |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : chern F                                       |
|                                                   |
|              1 2         1 3                      |
|o3 = 1 + c + (-c  - d) + (-c  - c*d)               |
|              2           6                        |
|                                                   |
|o3 : QQ[c..d]                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : integral oo                                   |
|                                                   |
|              1 3                                  |
|o4 = integral(-c  - c*d)                           |
|              6                                    |
|                                                   |
|o4 : Expression of class Adjacent                  |
+---------------------------------------------------+

