Correspondence -- the class of all correspondences
**************************************************

Description
===========

A correspondence $I$ from from an *note AbstractVariety: AbstractVariety, $X$
(the *note source: (Macaulay2Doc)source, of $I$) to another AbstractVariety $Y$
(the *note target: (Macaulay2Doc)target, of $I$) consists of two functions
$I_*$ and $I^*$, which take cycles on $X$ to cycles on $Y$ and vice-versa,
respectively.  In general these functions are not ring maps or even module
maps.  See *note Correspondence ^*: Correspondence ^_st, and *note
Correspondence _*: Correspondence _us_st, for more info.

Unlike an *note IncidenceCorrespondence: IncidenceCorrespondence,, a general
Correspondence need not have an intermediate variety.

Types of Correspondence:
========================

  * *note IncidenceCorrespondence: IncidenceCorrespondence, -- the class of all
    incidence correspondences

Functions and methods returning an object of class Correspondence:
==================================================================

  * *note Correspondence * Correspondence: Correspondence _st Correspondence,
    -- composition of correspondences
  * *note transpose(Correspondence): transpose_lpCorrespondence_rp, -- reverse
    the direction of a correspondence

Methods that use an object of class Correspondence:
===================================================

  * *note Correspondence ^*: Correspondence ^_st, -- pullback along a
    correspondence
  * *note Correspondence _*: Correspondence _us_st, -- pushforward along a
    correspondence
  * *note source(Correspondence): source_lpCorrespondence_rp, -- the source of
    a correspondence
  * *note target(Correspondence): target_lpCorrespondence_rp, -- the target of
    a correspondence

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Correspondence: Correspondence, is a *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type,, with ancestor classes *note MutableHashTable:
(Macaulay2Doc)MutableHashTable, < *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, <
*note Thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,.

