flagBundle -- make a flag bundle
********************************

  * Usage: 
        flagBundle(r,E)
  * Inputs:
      * r, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list $\{r_0, ..., r_{n-1}\}$ of
        non-negative integers
      * E, an *note abstract sheaf: AbstractSheaf,, whose flag bundle is to be
        formed. If $E$ is, instead, an *note abstract variety: AbstractVariety,
        then a trivial sheaf on it is used. If $E$ is, instead, an *note
        integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, then a trivial sheaf on *note point: point,
        of rank $E$ is used. If $E$ is omitted, then a trivial sheaf on *note
        point: point, is used; its rank is the sum of the entries of $r$.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableNames => a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, default value
        null, used for specifying how the generators of the intersection ring
        of the resulting flag bundle are to be named. If no value is provided,
        then H_(i,j) = $H_{i,j}$ denotes the j-th Chern class of i-th
        tautological sheaf. If its value is a symbol, then that symbol is used
        instead of H. If its value is a list, then for each i, its i-th entry
        specifies how the Chern classes of the i-th tautological sheaf are to
        be named. If the i-th entry is omitted (i.e., is *note null:
        (Macaulay2Doc)null,), then the default names are used. If the i-th
        entry is a symbol, say c, then the names are c_1 .. c_(r_i). If the
        i-th entry is a string, say c, then the names are c1, c2, c3, ... . If
        the i-th entry is a list, its entries are used as the names.
      * QuotientBundles => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true, whether the additional tautological subquotient
        bundle, needed to make up the discrepancy between the sum of the rank
        specified by $r$ and the rank of $E$, should be at the bottom of the
        filtration.
      * Isotropic => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether to produce the isotropic flag bundle; in that
        case, the vector bundle should have even rank.
  * Outputs:
      * F, an *note abstract flag bundle: FlagBundle,, the flag bundle over the
        variety of $E$ parametrizing filtrations $0 = E_0 \subseteq{} E_1
        \subseteq{} ... \subseteq{} E_n = E$ of $E$ whose successive
        subquotients are vector bundles $E_{i+1}/E_i$ of rank $r_i$
  * Consequences:
      * The list r of ranks can be obtained later with F.BundleRanks, see *note
        BundleRanks: BundleRanks,. Its sum can be obtained with F.Rank.
      * The list of consecutive quotients in the tautological filtration can be
        obtained later with bundles F, see *note bundles: bundles,. See also
        *note SubBundles: SubBundles, and *note QuotientBundles:
        QuotientBundles,.
      * The (relative) tautological line bundle can be obtained later with
        OO_F(1).
      * The structure map from F to the variety of E can be obtained later with
        F.StructureMap, see *note StructureMap: StructureMap,. Abstract sheaves
        and cycle classes can be pulled back and pushed forward, see *note
        AbstractVarietyMap ^*: AbstractVarietyMap ^_st, and  *note
        AbstractVarietyMap _*: AbstractVarietyMap _us_st,.  Integration will
        work if it works on the variety of E, see *note integral: integral,.
        The (relative) tangent bundle can be obtained from it, see *note
        tangentBundle(AbstractVarietyMap): tangentBundle,.

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : base(3,Bundle => (E,4,c))                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = a variety                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : an abstract variety of dimension 3                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = flagBundle({2,2},E)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = F                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {2:2}                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : bundles F                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = (a sheaf, a sheaf)                                                      |
|                                                                             |
