IncidenceCorrespondence -- the class of all incidence correspondences
*********************************************************************

Description
===========

An incidence correspondence $I$ is a correspondence from an *note
AbstractVariety: AbstractVariety, $X$ (the *note source: (Macaulay2Doc)source,
of $I$) to another AbstractVariety $Y$ (the *note target: (Macaulay2Doc)target,
of $I$) which is mediated by a third AbstractVariety $Z$, together with *note
AbstractVarietyMap: AbstractVarietyMap,s $f:Z\rightarrow X$ and $g:Z\rightarrow
Y$.

Given a cycle $x$ on $X$, the pushforward of $x$ along $I$ is $$I_* x = g_* f^*
x,$$ and similarly for bundles on $X$.  Likewise, if $y$ is a cycle on $Y$, the
pullback of $y$ along $I$ is $$I^* y = f_* g^* y,$$ and similarly for bundles
on $Y$.  See *note Correspondence ^*: Correspondence ^_st, and *note
Correspondence _*: Correspondence _us_st, for more info.

The tuple $(Z,f,g)$ can be accessed via the *note intermediates: intermediates,
command.

Functions and methods returning an incidence correspondence:
============================================================

  * *note incidenceCorrespondence: incidenceCorrespondence, -- build
    containment correspondence between two Grassmannians
  * "transpose(IncidenceCorrespondence)" -- see *note
    transpose(Correspondence): transpose_lpCorrespondence_rp, -- reverse the
    direction of a correspondence

Methods that use an incidence correspondence:
=============================================

  * "intermediates(IncidenceCorrespondence)" -- see *note intermediates:
    intermediates,

