inclusion -- build the freest possible inclusion map
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        inclusion(f, NormalClass => c, Codimension => r, SuperTangent => tY, SuperDimension => dY, Base => S)
        inclusion(f, SubTangent => tX, SubDimension => dX, SuperTangent => tY, SuperDimension => dY)
        inclusion(f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, from A to B; we think of A as part of the Chow ring of Y and B as
        part of the Chow ring of X
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Codimension => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null,
        the codimension of X in Y
      * SubDimension => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        null, the dimension of X
      * SuperDimension => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        null, the dimension of Y
      * SubTangent => a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, default
        value null, element of B, the Chern class of the tangent bundle of X
      * SuperTangent => a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,,
        default value null, element of A, the Chern class of the tangent bundle
        of Y
      * NormalClass => a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,,
        default value null, element of B, the Chern class of the normal bundle
        of X in Y
      * Base => a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, default value null, a Ring
        or AbstractVariety, the base ring/variety to work over
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract variety map: AbstractVarietyMap,, the natural map
        from X to Z.
  * Consequences:
      * An *note extensionAlgebra: extensionAlgebra, of A by B is built, with
        normal class equal to the degree-r part of c.  This algebra is made
        into the ring of a variety Z, see *note abstractVariety:
        abstractVariety_lpZZ_cmRing_rp,.  A tangent class is installed on Z,
        see *note tangentBundle: tangentBundle,.  If A and B each have an *note
        integral: integral, defined, then an integral is defined on the
        coordinate ring of Z, and a *note StructureMap: StructureMap, is
        installed on Z.
      * A variety X for B is built if B is not already the ring of a variety,
        see *note abstractVariety: abstractVariety_lpZZ_cmRing_rp,.  A tangent
        class is installed on X if it does not already have one, see *note
        tangentBundle: tangentBundle,.  A *note StructureMap: StructureMap, is
        installed if B already has an *note integral: integral, defined.
      * If Base option is used, the supplied ring is made into the ring of a
        variety, if it is not already one.

Description
===========

Given the pullback map f from A to B, builds the freest possible extension E of
A by B (see *note extensionAlgebra: extensionAlgebra,), and then adds
appropriate metadata to make the maps from E to B and vice-versa into an *note
AbstractVarietyMap: AbstractVarietyMap,.  Enough information must be given to
compute the dimensions of X and Y, either by using the SubDimension,
SuperDimension, and Codimension options, or by having varieties already
attached to A and/or B.  Likewise, enough information must be given to compute
the tangent classes of X and Y.

This construction is useful for computations where the pullback map is known
but the pushforward is either not known or cannot be defined.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : p = point                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = point                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : an abstract variety of dimension 0                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = intersectionRing p                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Y = projectiveBundle(5,p)                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Y                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {1, 5}                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A = intersectionRing Y                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : B = S[h, Join => false]/h^3 -- A^*(P2), but using 2 times a line as the |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : QuotientRing                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|generating class:                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : integral B := (b) -> (4 * coefficient((B_0)^2, b))                      |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = FunctionClosure[currentString:6:14-6:50]                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : FunctionClosure                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : c = 1 + (9/2)*h + (15/2)*h^2 -- normal class                            |
|                                                                             |
|     15 2   9                                                                |
|o7 = --h  + -h + 1                                                           |
|      2     2                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : B                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : f = map(B,A,{-h, h, h^2, h^3, h^4, h^5})                                |
|                                                                             |
|                         2                                                   |
|o8 = map (B, A, {-h, h, h , 0, 0, 0})                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : RingMap B <-- A                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : i = inclusion(f,                                                        |
|         NormalClass => c,                                                   |
|         Codimension => 3,                                                   |
|         Base => p) -- Base not necessary, will be correctly computed        |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = i                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : a map to a variety from a variety                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : Z = target i                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = Z                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : an abstract variety of dimension 5                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : X = source i                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = X                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : an abstract variety of dimension 2                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : Xstruct = X / point                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = Xstruct                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : a map to point from X                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : rank Xstruct_* tangentBundle X                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o13 = 8                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : integral chern tangentBundle Z                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = 6                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o14 : S                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

