integral -- compute an integral (push forward a cycle to the base)
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        integral f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a cycle class in
        the intersection ring of an abstract variety
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the integral of $f$.

Description
===========

In this example we compute the number of lines meeting four lines in space.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = flagBundle {2,2}                      |
|                                               |
|o1 = G                                         |
|                                               |
|o1 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {2:2}|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : dim G                                     |
|                                               |
|o2 = 4                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : A = intersectionRing G                    |
|                                               |
|o3 = A                                         |
|                                               |
|o3 : QuotientRing                              |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = (chern_1 OO_G(1))^4                   |
|                                               |
|       2                                       |
|o4 = 2H                                        |
|       2,2                                     |
|                                               |
|o4 : A                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : integral f                                |
|                                               |
|o5 = 2                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+

Normally this integral will be an element of the intersection ring of *note
point: point,, and thus will essentially be a rational number, but it could be
in any base variety, and would be obtained by pushing forward along the
structure maps of flag bundles until the (ultimate) base variety is reached.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : pt = base n                               |
|                                               |
|o6 = pt                                        |
|                                               |
|o6 : an abstract variety of dimension 0        |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : F = flagBundle_{2,2} pt                   |
|                                               |
|o7 = F                                         |
|                                               |
|o7 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {2:2}|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : integral (chern_1 OO_F(n))^4              |
|                                               |
|       4                                       |
|o8 = 2n                                        |
|                                               |
|o8 : QQ[n]                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+

