map(FlagBundle,AbstractVarietyMap,List) -- make a map from an abstract variety to a flag bundle
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        map(F,f,b)
        map(F,X,b)
  * Inputs:
      * F, an *note abstract flag bundle: FlagBundle,, over a variety S, of the
        form $flagBundle(\{r_0, ..., r_{n-1}\},E)$, say, where $E$ is an
        abstract sheaf on $S$
      * an *note abstract variety map: AbstractVarietyMap,, f, an *note
        abstract variety map: AbstractVarietyMap, from a variety $X$, say, to
        $S$; or X, an *note abstract variety: AbstractVariety,, with a
        structure map $f : X \rightarrow{} S$
      * b, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of the form $\{B_0,...B_{n-1}\}$
        whose elements are abstract sheaves on X, with $rank B_i = r_i$, for
        each i. The sheaves should be effective in the sense that $c_j B_i = 0$
        for $j > r_i$. The sum of the sheaves should equal $f^* E$;
        alternatively, one of them can be omitted and it will be deduced from
        the condition on the sum.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, the value of this option is ignored
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, the value of this option is ignored
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, the value of this option is ignored
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract variety map: AbstractVarietyMap,, the map of abstract
        varieties $g : X \rightarrow{} F$ over $S$ such that $g^* (E_{i+1}/E_i)
        = B_i$, for each i, where $0 = E_0 \subseteq{} E_1 \subseteq{} ...
