schubertCycle -- compute Schubert Cycles on a Grassmannian, Fulton-style
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        schubertCycle(s,F)
  * Inputs:
      * F, an *note abstract flag bundle: FlagBundle,, associated to a vector
        bundle $A$, say, of rank $n$. This flag bundle should be a
        Grassmannian, parametrizing rank $r$ sub-bundles of $A$, say.
      * s, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence, $(s_0, ..., s_{r-1})$ of
        length $r$ of integers, with $0 \le{} s_0 < ... < s_{r-1} < n$, or a
        *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,  $\{s_0, ..., s_{r-1}\}$ of length $r$
        of integers, with $n-r \ge{} s_0 \ge{} ... \ge{} s_{r-1} \ge{} 0$
  * Outputs:
      * c, the appropriate Schubert class or Schubert variety, depending on the
        type of s.  See page 271 of Fulton's book, Intersection Theory for the
        notations.  In the case where s is a a *note sequence:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, the value returned is the homology class of
        the Schubert variety in $ F $ consisting of those points corresponding
        to $(r-1)$-planes of $\PP(A)$ that meet $ W_j $ in dimension at least $
        i $ with $0 \le{} i < r-1$, for each $ i $, where $ j = s_i $, and
        where $ W_j $ is the projective subspace of dimension $ j $ in a fixed
        (complete) flag $0 = W_0 \subset{} W_1 \subset{} ... \subset{} W_{n-1}
        = \PP(A) $.  Here $ \PP(A) $ denotes the "Fulton-style"  projective
        bundle parametrizing rank 1 sub-bundles of $A$; for opposite
        "Grothendieck-style" version, see *note schubertCycle':
        schubertCycle',.  In the case where s is a a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the result is the corresponding Schubert class in
        cohomology.  In Schubert2 homology and cohomology are identified with
        each other. Given a sequence $(s_0, ..., s_{r-1})$, one can convert it
        to a list yielding the same Schubert class by the formula $ \{...,
        n-r+i-s_i, ...\} $.

Description
===========

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : base(0, Bundle=>(A, n=8, a))               |
|                                                |
|o1 = a variety                                  |
|                                                |
|o1 : an abstract variety of dimension 0         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : F = flagBundle ({r=5,3},A)                 |
|                                                |
|o2 = F                                          |
|                                                |
|o2 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {5, 3}|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : CH = intersectionRing F;                   |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : schubertCycle((0,1,5,6,7),F)               |
|                                                |
|      2                                         |
|o4 = H                                          |
|      2,3                                       |
|                                                |
|o4 : CH                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : {n-r+0-0,n-r+1-1,n-r+2-5,n-r+3-6,n-r+4-7}  |
|                                                |
|o5 = {3, 3, 0, 0, 0}                            |
|                                                |
|o5 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : schubertCycle(oo,F)                        |
|                                                |
|      2                                         |
|o6 = H                                          |
|      2,3                                       |
|                                                |
|o6 : CH                                         |
+------------------------------------------------+

