TautologicalLineBundle -- a symbol used internally as a key
***********************************************************

Description
===========

If $X$ is an abstract variety and its tautological line bundle has already been
built, it is stored in X.TautologicalLineBundle.  However, because building
this bundle can be computationally intensive, it is often not built unless it
is requested by *note tautologicalLineBundle: tautologicalLineBundle,.  The
programmer is warned not to make direct reference to this key for this reason.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : X = abstractProjectiveSpace 3                             |
|                                                               |
|o1 = X                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o1 : a flag bundle with subquotient ranks {1, 3}               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : try X.TautologicalLineBundle else print "bundle not found"|
|bundle not found                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : L = tautologicalLineBundle X                              |
|                                                               |
|o3 = L                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o3 : an abstract sheaf of rank 1 on X                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : L === X.TautologicalLineBundle                            |
|                                                               |
|o4 = true                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : rank L                                                    |
|                                                               |
|o5 = 1                                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : chern L                                                   |
|                                                               |
|o6 = 1 + H                                                     |
|          2,1                                                  |
|                                                               |
|                       QQ[][h, H   ..H   ]                     |
|                                2,1   2,3                      |
|o6 : -------------------------------------------------------   |
|     (- h - H   , - h*H    - H   , - h*H    - H   , -h*H   )   |
|             2,1       2,1    2,2       2,2    2,3      2,3    |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

Here are the preferred ways to get the tautological line bundle:

+-------------------------------------+
|i7 : OO_X(1)                         |
|                                     |
|o7 = L                               |
|                                     |
|o7 : an abstract sheaf of rank 1 on X|
+-------------------------------------+
|i8 : L === oo                        |
|                                     |
|o8 = true                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i9 : tautologicalLineBundle X        |
|                                     |
|o9 = L                               |
|                                     |
|o9 : an abstract sheaf of rank 1 on X|
+-------------------------------------+
|i10 : L === oo                       |
|                                     |
|o10 = true                           |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note tautologicalLineBundle: tautologicalLineBundle, -- get the
    tautological line bundle of a flag bundle or abstract variety

